@* 
    Make our view as a strongly typed view which we are returning from the Controller, 
    that is bound to list of string. You can also bind to predefined classes or interfaces as well.
    IEnumerable is the parent interface of the List class. So, it is recommended to mention the interface name
    as the model class name here. Because in future, you may change your mind.
    You may return a List or any other child of the IEnumerable. 
    Maybe for example, a dictionary or anything like that. But still, this data type should work.
    Thats the benifit.
    So, finally, the model property here refers to a list of string that was supplied from the service.
    Below we are looping over the data.
*@
@model IEnumerable<string>
@{
    ViewBag.Title = "Home";
}
<h1>Cities</h1>
<ul class="list">
    @foreach (string city in Model)
    {
        <li>@city</li>
    }
</ul>